#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Refuse to commit onto a detached HEAD.
#
# `ops/smoke.sh` also checks this, and checking it there is too late. A peer
# session reviewing commits by checking them out IN THIS CLONE detached HEAD
# five times on 2026-08-18/19. Each time, `git push origin main` then pushed the
# unchanged branch and exited 0, so five commits were reported as pushed while
# reachable only from here.
#
# The near miss is worse than the miss, and it is telemetry's point: recovery
# was a fast-forward only because the sha they happened to leave HEAD on was
# AHEAD of main. They had also checked out 6f258d2, an older one. A commit
# landing there does not fast-forward; `git checkout main` would have left it
# reachable only from the reflog, and a smoke check would have reported the
# problem after the commit was already orphaned.
#
# So this refuses at the point the commit is created, which is the last moment
# prevention is still available.
#
# Enable (per clone, not carried by git):
#     git config core.hooksPath githooks
#
# Bypass deliberately, when a detached commit is what you actually want:
#     git commit --no-verify
# `git symbolic-ref -q HEAD`, NOT `rev-parse --abbrev-ref HEAD`.
#
# rev-parse prints the literal string "HEAD" for an UNBORN branch as well as a
# detached one, and this hook read its stdout while ignoring its exit code — so
# the very first commit in a fresh repo was refused with a message blaming a
# peer for a checkout nobody had done. That is the fabricated-reason defect
# (a refusal asserting a cause it cannot know) reappearing inside the layer
# written to prevent that family. Found by timepoint-telemetry, whose test
# harness was itself a fresh repo.
#
#   state      rev-parse --abbrev-ref    symbolic-ref -q
#   unborn     "HEAD", exit 128          exit 0    <- a branch; a commit here reaches main
#   branch     "main", exit 0            exit 0
#   detached   "HEAD", exit 0            exit 1
#
# An unborn branch IS a branch. symbolic-ref separates all three with no
# stdout parsing and no exit-code ambiguity.
if ! git symbolic-ref -q HEAD >/dev/null; then
    cat >&2 <<'MSG'
refusing: HEAD is DETACHED.

A commit here will not reach origin/main, and `git push origin main` will
report success while pushing the branch you are not on.

    git checkout main          # then re-run the commit
    git commit --no-verify     # if a detached commit is genuinely intended

If you did not detach it, a peer session probably reviewed a commit by checking
it out in this clone. Ask them to use `git show <sha>:<path>` or their own clone.
MSG
    exit 1
fi
